Description: Beautiful CLI network diagnostics
 xping provides live, colour-coded output for ping, traceroute, MTR,
 DNS (including propagation checks), TLS, HTTP, WHOIS, port scanning,
 health scoring, speed testing, and more, over IPv4 and IPv6. Ping and
 traceroute work without root on Linux via unprivileged ICMP sockets.
 .
 Every command returns a meaningful exit code and accepts thresholds,
 so it can be used from scripts and monitoring; batch checks run from a
 TOML/JSON file. Includes bash/zsh/fish completion and JSON/CSV/Markdown
 export on every command.
